.claude
**/.env
**/.venv/
notes.md
text-survey.md
survey-results.md
plan.md
sources.md
roadmap.md
NOTES.md
processing-new-texts.md
adding-new-supplements.md
format-standards.md
site/node_modules/
site/public/text-index.json
mcp/node_modules/
mcp/dist/
mcp/.wrangler/
**/__pycache__/
.DS_Store
site/public/toc/

# Proofreading: derived artifacts only. Briefs, findings and ledgers ARE tracked.
ocr/4-proofread/*/pagemap.json
ocr/4-proofread/*/batches/

# Dispatch runs: the record is tracked, the transcript is not.
# NOTES.md is the point of a run, and a global NOTES.md rule above was
# silently swallowing it -- the findings are the deliverable, not debris.
ocr/runs/*/run.log
ocr/runs/*/workspace/
!ocr/runs/*/NOTES.md

# The adopted text and its images live under texts/. A run that has been adopted
# was keeping a byte-identical second copy of both, which git then kept forever:
# ~14.6 MB across four adoptions, and the same again on every future one.
#
# WHITELIST -- and note that this repo has been bitten by a whitelist before.
# dispatch-text.sh once listed the source types to copy and would have silently
# withheld a .tex nobody anticipated, which is why it is a blacklist today. The
# same hazard applies here: a NEW kind of record file, dropped into a run
# directory by a future worker, will be ignored silently rather than tracked.
# If you add one, add it here too. Better still, teach adopt-run.py to warn when
# a run holds a .md that is neither whitelisted below nor the adopted candidate.
ocr/runs/*/*.md
ocr/runs/*/images/
# NOTES.md is negated AGAIN here, deliberately. The negation twelve lines above
# is not enough: gitignore takes the LAST matching rule, so the broad *.md
# ignore just added would re-swallow the one file this section exists to keep --
# the identical failure the comment above records. Order is the whole rule.
!ocr/runs/*/NOTES.md
!ocr/runs/*/TASK.md
!ocr/runs/*/BRIEF.md
!ocr/runs/*/PROPOSED.md
!ocr/runs/*/CLOSED.md
!ocr/runs/*/ESCALATION.md
!ocr/runs/*/ANSWER.md
